## Phase 1: GitHub rename existing repos

Repos that exist on GitHub and need renaming:

```bash
gh repo rename tgbot-module-antispam -R bagart/telegram-bot-antispam-module -y
gh repo rename tgbot-module-nettools -R bagart/telegram-bot-nettools-module -y
gh repo rename tgbot-module-proxy -R bagart/telegram-bot-proxy-module -y
gh repo rename tgbot-module-stt -R bagart/telegram-bot-stt-module -y
gh repo rename tgbot-module-summarizer -R bagart/telegram-bot-summarizer-module -y
gh repo rename tgbot-module-tts -R bagart/telegram-bot-tts-module -y
gh repo rename tgbot-game-mafia -R bagart/telegram-game-mafia -y
gh repo rename telegram-bot-lib-access -R bagart/telegram-bot-access-module -y
gh repo rename telegram-bot-lib-basic -R bagart/telegram-bot-basic-lib -y
gh repo rename telegram-platform-management -R bagart/telegram-bot-management -y
gh repo rename telegram-platform-devops-baseline -R bagart/telegram-devops-baseline -y
```

## Phase 2: GitHub create new repos

Repos that don't exist on GitHub yet:

```bash
gh repo create bagart/tgbot-module-audit --public
gh repo create bagart/tgbot-module-example --public
gh repo create bagart/telegram-platform-menu --public
```

## Phase 3: Local git origin update (before dir rename)

```bash
# Modules
git -C misc/BAGArt/telegram-bot-antispam-module remote set-url origin git@github.com:bagart/tgbot-module-antispam.git
git -C misc/BAGArt/telegram-bot-nettools-module remote set-url origin git@github.com:bagart/tgbot-module-nettools.git
git -C misc/BAGArt/telegram-bot-proxy-module remote set-url origin git@github.com:bagart/tgbot-module-proxy.git
git -C misc/BAGArt/telegram-bot-stt-module remote set-url origin git@github.com:bagart/tgbot-module-stt.git
git -C misc/BAGArt/telegram-bot-summarizer-module remote set-url origin git@github.com:bagart/tgbot-module-summarizer.git
git -C misc/BAGArt/telegram-bot-tts-module remote set-url origin git@github.com:bagart/tgbot-module-tts.git

# Exceptions
git -C misc/BAGArt/telegram-game-mafia remote set-url origin git@github.com:bagart/tgbot-game-mafia.git
git -C misc/BAGArt/telegram-bot-basic-lib remote set-url origin git@github.com:bagart/telegram-bot-lib-basic.git
git -C misc/BAGArt/telegram-bot-management remote set-url origin git@github.com:bagart/telegram-platform-management.git
git -C misc/BAGArt/telegram-devops-baseline remote set-url origin git@github.com:bagart/telegram-platform-devops-baseline.git

# Init + add remote for repos without git
cd misc/BAGArt/telegram-bot-access-module && git init && git remote add origin git@github.com:bagart/telegram-bot-lib-access.git
cd misc/BAGArt/telegram-bot-audit-module && git init && git remote add origin git@github.com:bagart/telegram-platform-audit.git
cd misc/BAGArt/telegram-bot-example-module && git init && git remote add origin git@github.com:bagart/tgbot-module-example.git
cd misc/BAGArt/telegram-bot-menu-module && git init && git remote add origin git@github.com:bagart/telegram-platform-menu.git
cd misc/BAGArt/telegram-module-engine && git remote add origin git@github.com:bagart/telegram-module-engine.git
```

## Phase 4: Local directory rename

```bash
cd misc/BAGArt

# Modules
git mv telegram-bot-antispam-module tgbot-module-antispam
git mv telegram-bot-audit-module telegram-platform-audit
git mv telegram-bot-example-module tgbot-module-example
git mv telegram-bot-menu-module telegram-platform-menu
git mv telegram-bot-nettools-module tgbot-module-nettools
git mv telegram-bot-proxy-module tgbot-module-proxy
git mv telegram-bot-stt-module tgbot-module-stt
git mv telegram-bot-summarizer-module tgbot-module-summarizer
git mv telegram-bot-tts-module tgbot-module-tts

# Exceptions
git mv telegram-game-mafia tgbot-game-mafia
git mv telegram-bot-access-module telegram-bot-lib-access
git mv telegram-bot-basic-lib telegram-bot-lib-basic
git mv telegram-bot-management telegram-platform-management
git mv telegram-devops-baseline telegram-platform-devops-baseline
```

For dirs without git: plain `mv`.

## Phase 5: Update references

After rename, update all references across the codebase:

1. **composer.json** (root + per-module) — PSR-4 namespaces, path repositories, autoload
2. **config/tg_modules.php** — module paths, namespace references
3. **config/telegram.php** — any module path references
4. **bootstrap/providers.php** — if any providers reference old paths
5. **routes/web.php** — if any routes reference module paths
6. **README.md / docs/** — all documentation references
7. **AGENTS.md** — project conventions section (module list)
8. **scripts/sync-skills.sh** — if it references module paths
9. **cmd/deps/** scripts — composer path repo references
10. **phpunit.xml** — test suite paths
11. **vite.config.js** — if any module frontend paths are referenced
12. **Docker/docker-compose** — if any volume mounts reference old paths
13. **Internal module cross-references** — one module requiring another via path repo

## Phase 6: Verification

```bash
# Check no old names remain in tracked files
grep -r "telegram-bot-antispam-module\|telegram-bot-audit-module\|telegram-bot-nettools-module" --include="*.php" --include="*.json" --include="*.md" .

# Verify all origins point to new names
for dir in misc/BAGArt/*/; do
  echo "=== $(basename $dir) ==="
  git -C "$dir" remote -v 2>/dev/null | grep origin || echo "NO REMOTE"
done

# Run tests
php artisan test --compact
```
